I downloaded and burned the beta image from Dec 99 and created it.  I booted

from the CD on a SPARC 10.  The install began to load, and after
initializing the hardware the install crashed with 
a bug listing, saying that the kernal timer had attempted to start twice at
a specified 
memory address (I would tell you what the address was but my documentation
is at 
home.  If you have not had this reported and need that info I would be happy
to 
provide it).  Thanks.
 
Keith Starks

